$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of S- and -S-(CH2)n-S-Substituted
Polyhalodienes-General Procedure I 4.00 g (15.33 mmol) 1 in 25 mL of EtOH
and 2.46 g (31.49 mmol) of the respective thiol in 25 mL of EtOH were
mixed and 1.32 g NaOH in 10 mL of water was added at room temperature.
The mixture was stirred for 24 h. Then CHCl3 (20 mL) was added to the
reaction mixture. The organic layer was separated, washed with water (4 x
30 mL), and dried with MgSO4. The solvent was evaporated and the residue
was purified by column chromatography on silica gel with CHCl3 as eluent.
2a [15], 2b, 2c, 4a-g, 5a, and 5b were synthesized in the same way.
1,2,3,4,4-Pentachloro-1-[6-(2-hydroxyethylthio)hexylthio]-1,3-butadiene
(4f) Yield: 0.42 g (95%); oil. Rf = 0.68 (hexane). IR (film): 3404 cm-1
(OH), 2931, 2856 cm-1 (C-H), 1601, 1544 (C = C). 1H NMR: 1.39-1.51 (m,
4H, SCH2CH2(CH2)2CH2S), 1.55-1.71 (m, 4H, SCH2CH2(CH2)2CH2S), 2.14-2.19
(t, 1H, OH), 2.50-2.56 (t, 2H, CH2S(CH2)2OH), 2.70-2.76 (t, 2H,
SCH2CH2OH), 2.93-3.04 (m, 2H, SCH2(CH2)5S), 3.70-3.78 (m, 2H, CH2OH).
Anal. calc. for C12H17Cl5S2O (418.66): C, 34.43; H, 4.09; S 15.32 found
C, 34.84; H, 3.94; S 15.21.
